FAIL GROUNDS — Criterion 6 (re-pinned test faithfulness):
TestKPIsTotalExpensesTile_RefundDominantRangeRendersSignedNegative in
internal/handlers/dashboard/verdict_render_test.go is a PURE ADDITION by
this merge commit (`git diff HEAD^1 HEAD -- .../verdict_render_test.go`
shows it added wholesale, not modified from either parent) — squarely in
the reconciliation's own scope, exactly the kind of re-pinned CB7 test
criterion 6 asks me to check.

It does NOT actually assert the sign-aware color behavior it claims to
pin. Proven by mutation: I edited kpis.html's Expenses-tile line from
  {{if gt .Metrics.TotalExpenses 0.0}}text-negative{{else}}text-positive{{end}}
to a hardcoded
  text-negative
(i.e. reverted the CB7 sign-aware color fix on the dashboard's main KPI
tile, the exact regression this test's own doc comment says it exists to
catch) and reran:
  go test ./internal/handlers/dashboard/... -run TestKPIsTotalExpensesTile_RefundDominantRangeRendersSignedNegative -v
Result: --- PASS. The test still passes with the color-only revert in
place. (File restored immediately after, confirmed byte-identical via
diff against the pre-edit backup; scratch copy only, real worktree never
touched.)

Root cause: the test only checks `strings.Contains(out, "text-positive")`
against the WHOLE rendered "kpis" partial, not scoped to the Expenses
tile's own `<p>`. kpis.html unconditionally renders the Total Income tile
with a literal `text-2xl font-bold text-positive` class (kpis.html:8) in
the SAME render call, so "text-positive" is present in the output
regardless of what color class the Expenses tile itself gets. The other
two assertions in the same test (`-$1,234.56` present, `>$1,234.56<`
absent) are unaffected by a color-only revert and so don't catch it
either.

This is exactly the failure mode the task's criterion 6 warns against
("confirm... that a color-only revert would still fail them") — and the
answer for this specific test is no, it would not. Contrast with the
explorer.js sibling tests (handlers_test.go:1516-1521), which correctly
scope the assertion to `text-positive ml-1">-$400.00` (color+value fused
in one substring) and separately assert the ROSE class's absence at that
same value — those are faithful and DO fail on the same class of revert
(verified by reading, not just inspection, given the fused-substring
pattern leaves no root for the Income-tile literal to leak through).

Remedy (fixes the diagnosed defect, satisfies self-check 6b): tighten the
new dashboard test to assert on the fused substring
`text-positive">-$1,234.56` (mirroring the explorer pattern) and add the
negative-of-that assertion (`text-negative">-$1,234.56` absent). I did not
apply this — read-only checker.

BACKLOG FINDINGS (real, but pre-existing in the U-run BEFORE this merge —
`git diff HEAD^1 HEAD` touches neither file at either location; confirmed
identical content already present at a61dc08, the tip of the U-run branch
this reconciliation merged FROM — so out of the RECONCILE task's scope
per constitution "could the worker have fixed this without exceeding
their task block"):

1. shared/range-picker.html's dynamic preset buttons are dead sitewide.
   `{{$.PresetAttr}}="{{.Value}}"` puts a template action in an HTML
   ATTRIBUTE NAME position; Go's html/template auto-escaper refuses this
   and emits the literal placeholder `ZgotmplZ="<value>"` instead of e.g.
   `data-months="3"`. Confirmed on the LIVE server: curl of /dashboard,
   /explorer, /major-expenses all show `ZgotmplZ="..."` where data-months/
   data-preset should be. explorer.js/major-expenses.js both select
   `.date-range-btn[data-months]` to attach click listeners — that
   selector matches zero elements, so the 1M/2M/3M/6M/12M/All preset
   buttons on Dashboard, Explorer, Major Expenses, and Insights do
   nothing when clicked. No test in internal/ asserts on `data-months`
   presence. This is severe (core UI feature dead across 4 pages) and
   present unchanged since a61dc08 (U7/U8 authored this partial) — flag
   for the U-run backlog, not this reconciliation.
2. Explorer's sortable `<th data-sort-key>` column headers (date,
   description, category, majorExpense, amount, ...) have no tabindex,
   role, or keydown handling — explorer.js:439-442 attaches only a click
   listener. Mouse-only; not reachable or operable by keyboard, contrary
   to the general U7 "keyboard-operable" intent for interactive controls.
   Identical in a61dc08; the merge's only touch to explorer.html was the
   CB7 Expenses-chip lines (git diff HEAD^1 HEAD -- explorer.html shows a
   4-line hunk, nowhere near the thead). Out of RECONCILE's scope.

SCOPE NOTE: the FAIL above (criterion-6 test gap) is the only defect I'm
treating as grounds for FAIL, because it is code the merge worker
